        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: поход",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "поход (pokhód) — \"a hike, a trek; a campaign\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Летом мы ходили в поход в горы. Létom my khodíli v pokhód v góry. In summer we went on a hike in the mountains."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine. Идти в поход (pokhód) — to go hiking or camping."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "поход (pokhód) is built from по- and ход 'a going', which is inherited from Proto-Slavic xodŭ 'motion' (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
